# Bot2's Steel Wall blocks Memnite on turn 3. On turn 5 Combat Celebrant's exertion adds a combat phase: in the first the
# Wall blocks a Warrior token, and Glyph of Reincarnation can't yet be cast in that combat's end of combat step; in the second
# it blocks Phyrexian Walker, and in that combat's end of combat step - after the turn's first combat (CR 506.8, 506.8d) - Bot1
# casts the Glyph at the Wall. The token and Phyrexian Walker, blocked this turn in either combat, die; Memnite, blocked only on
# an earlier turn, does not. Two died, so two creature cards come from Bot1's graveyard, both at once: Phyrexian Walker, the
# very creature just destroyed (the 2004-10-04 ruling), and Ornithopter, which Bot2 bolted. The token is in that graveyard
# until the state-based actions, but it is no card (CR 111.1, 704.5d) and can't be chosen.
[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Combat Celebrant
Memnite
Phyrexian Walker
Mox Pearl
Mox Emerald
Ornithopter
Secure the Wastes
Glyph of Reincarnation
Plains x20
[Bot2 Deck]
Steel Wall
Island
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Island x25
